        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Am I the only one who thinks that \"would\" is not a mechanic, but just the clearest way to write something?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The intent is unlcear at best. And as with all \"ambiguous\" situations, the rulebook leaves it up to player choice (though that rule probably was not writen with this application in mind).</p>\n<p>The clarification to Fort/SHD should really point us in the right direction with how to best interpret \"would\" found in trigger clauses.</p>\n<p>(<a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/christopher\">@Christopher</a>, we are ready for that whenever you are!  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/innocent.png?v=12\" title=\":innocent:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":innocent:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> )</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:59:31.982Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
